"Veo 3"],modules:[{type:"hero",content:{date:"Feb 20, 2026",headline:"Holywater accelerates creative production for AI entertainment using Veo 3 and Gemini 2.5 Pro",Zq:"Holywater scales content analysis and creation by integrating Gemini Pro and Veo models into video production workflows for My Drama, an award-winning AI video streaming app.",De:[{name:"Anatolii Kasianov",role:"Co-CEO and Co-Founder, Holywater"}],thumbnail:{src:"https://www.gstatic.com/aistudio/case_studies/holywater/holywater_hero.jpg",
type:"image",alt:"Holywater showcase hero"}}},{type:"stats",content:{stats:[{value:"55M+",description:"users"},{value:"18%",description:"higher series completion rate vs. filmed series"},{value:"4-6",description:"new series releases per month"}]}},{type:"cta",content:{link:"https://aistudio.google.com/prompts/new_chat?model=gemini-pro-latest"}},{type:"text",content:{body:'\n            <p>\n              <a href="https://www.holywater.tech/">Holywater</a> is an entertainment network that produces high-quality content using its powerful suite of AI tools. The company has specialized apps covering entertainment categories, including e-books, music, and vertical video with <a href="https://my-drama.com/">My Drama</a>. Its audience of over 55 million users has consumed a combined total of more than 100 million hours of content.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              To keep up with its continually growing audience, the Holywater team needed to rapidly scale its content analysis, content generation, and automation workflows. They selected <a href="https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/video">Veo 3</a> for its high-fidelity video generation and Gemini 2.5 Pro for its complex multimodal understanding, eliminating creative bottlenecks and accelerating video releases.\n            </p>'}},
{type:"video",content:{video:{Iea:!0,sources:[{url:"https://www.gstatic.com/aistudio/case_studies/holywater/holywater_demo_2.mp4",type:"video/mp4"}]}}},{type:"text",content:{header:{headline:"<h2>Enhanced content analysis and development with Gemini 2.5 Pro</h2>"},body:"\n            <p>\n              The Holywater team found that Gemini 2.5 Pro was more consistent and accurate at extracting structured insights from video content than other frontier models. So they began integrating the Gemini API and Google AI Studio into their workflows, with cofounder and co-CEO Anatolii Kasianov noting, \u201cThe first usable pipelines were running within a few days, and full operational adoption took less than two weeks.\u201d\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              The model helped the team accelerate their content analysis, as the model\u2019s 1 million token context window enables processing of subject matter\u2014such as an entire book series\u2014to understand nuanced elements like plot structure, character development, and emotional tone. It uses advanced reasoning to segment videos into scenes and extracts metadata such as emotional tones, visual cues, and overall context to provide structured insights for creative analysis and automation workflows.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              It then generates narrative structures, scripts, and campaigns. Automating this foundational analysis helps to enable the creatives at Holywater to focus on high-level tasks, such as overall quality control, content strategy, and brand alignment.\n            </p>"}},
{type:"quote",content:{quote:"After adopting Gemini 2.5 Pro , we saw a significantly faster time-to-production and the removal of manual work for simple or repetitive tasks. This allowed us to automate large parts of our workflow and free up human resources for more complex creative and analytical work.",author:"\u2014 Anatolii Kasianov, Co-CEO and Cofounder of Holywater"}},{type:"text",content:{header:{headline:"<h2>Delivering next-level visuals with Veo 3</h2>"},body:"\n            <p>\n              Veo 3 is Google's state-of-the-art model for generating high-fidelity video and audio, accessible through the Gemini API. To take its content creation to the next level, Holywater began implementing Veo 3 into its production pipeline, starting with its My Drama app.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              The team used Veo 3 to generate an entire series based on the structured inputs provided by Gemini 2.5 Pro. They saw early success in the true crime genre, where Veo 3 generated high-quality vertical video that achieved engagement metrics similar to filmed original content.\n            </p>"}},
{type:"images",content:{items:[{image:{src:"https://www.gstatic.com/aistudio/case_studies/holywater/series-completion-inline-original.png",alt:"Analytics show that Holywater\u2019s AI-generated series receives up to 22% higher completion rate than filmed series"}}]}},{type:"text",content:{header:{headline:"<h2>Reimagining the future of AI entertainment</h2>"},body:'\n            <p>\n              By automating content analysis and generation using Gemini and Veo models, Holywater is able to release 4-6 new entries each month and have the team focus on analytical tasks. The team is testing Gemini 3 Pro\u2019s video processing capabilities to analyze more frames per second and achieve an even deeper understanding of content.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              My Drama was the Webby Awards 2025 People\u2019s Voice Winner for Best Streaming Service and in October 2025, <a href="https://www.holywater.tech/blog/fox-entertainment-enters-a-strategic-partnership-with-holywater-to-drive-hollywoods-evolution-2">Fox Entertainment took an equity stake in Holywater</a>, committing to produce more than 200 titles for My Drama over the next 2 years. With the growing audience for vertical video, Hollywood is taking notice of ways to scale IP led content strategy. \u201cAI is at our core,\u201d said Kasianov. \u201cIt\u2019s not experimental; it\u2019s driving real business growth.\u201d\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              Read the Gemini API documentation to start building with <a href="https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/video?example=dialogue">Veo 3</a> and <a href="https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/models#gemini-2.5-pro">Gemini 2.5 Pro</a>.\n            </p>'}},
{type:"related_cases",content:{mf:["compscience","forio","fal"]}}]},{title:"Diia",Ue:"Diia.AI saves Ukrainian citizens hours navigating government processes and services with an accessible AI agent.",slug:"diia",zf:"https://aistudio.google.com/prompts/new_chat?model=gemini-flash-latest",thumbnail:{url:"https://www.gstatic.com/aistudio/case_studies/diia/diiaai_thumbnail.jpg",alt:"DIIA showcase preview"},se:["Gemini 2.0 Flash"],modules:[{type:"hero",content:{date:"February 6, 2025",headline:"The Ministry of Digital Transformation of Ukraine revolutionizes government services with Gemini 2.0 Flash",
Zq:"Diia.AI deploys conversational agents on Vertex AI to simplify government processes for Ukrainian citizens without compromising data privacy.",De:[{name:"Dmytro Ovcharenko",role:"CTO, WINWIN AI Center of Excellence & AI CTO, Ministry of Digital Transformation of Ukraine"}],thumbnail:{src:"https://www.gstatic.com/aistudio/case_studies/diia/diiaai_thumbnail.jpg",type:"image",alt:"Diia showcase hero"}}},{type:"cta",content:{link:"https://aistudio.google.com/prompts/new_chat?model=gemini-flash-latest"}},
{type:"text",content:{body:"\n          <p>\n            Diia is an online platform and app developed by the Ministry of Digital Transformation of Ukraine, offering over 23 million citizens digital access to 33 essential government documents\u2014including ID cards, driver's licenses, and passports\u2014and more than 150 services covering everything from traffic tickets to taxes. The platform\u2019s next phase is an AI-powered transformation: Diia.AI, an agent designed to proactively offer services and eliminate bureaucracy.\n          </p>\n          <p>\n            The team chose Gemini 2.0 Flash to build it due to its superior cost-efficiency and performance, and to host it via Vertex AI for maximum data security.\n          </p>"}},
{type:"video",content:{video:{sources:[{url:"https://www.gstatic.com/aistudio/case_studies/diia/diiaai_demo.mp4",type:"video/mp4"}],legend:"The Diia.AI chatbot interface shows a user requesting their insurance history and ordering an official income statement through an AI assistant."}}},{type:"text",content:{header:{headline:"<h2>Making government services accessible to over 23 million Ukrainian citizens</h2>"},body:"\n            <p>\n              Diia helps make government services accessible to everyone, regardless of technical literacy or familiarity with complex processes. Dmytro Ovcharenko, CTO at the WINWIN AI Center of Excellence and AI CTO at the Ministry of Digital Transformation of Ukraine, noted, \u201cOur goal is to make Diia accessible and useful to everyone, from students to entrepreneurs to pensioners.\u201d Integrating agentic AI into the platform would aid citizens in navigating both Diia and complex government forms and processes.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              Supporting a model of this magnitude in-house, however, was not feasible. After evaluating several cloud-based options, the team determined that Gemini 2.0 Flash would be the ideal solution for performance, scalability, and cost. The model needed to not only excel in conversational Ukrainian but also understand and generate complex legal and administrative phrasing. To ensure accuracy, it used Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) to access a constantly updated, validated knowledge base built from official Diia sources.\n            </p>"}},
{type:"quote",content:{quote:"Other high-performance, API-based models were financially prohibitive. Gemini 2.0 Flash showed really great results, delivering the speed and intelligence we needed at a cost that made the project viable.",author:"- Dmytro Ovcharenko<br><br>CTO at the WINWIN AI Center of Excellence and AI CTO at the Ministry of Digital Transformation of Ukraine"}},{type:"text",content:{body:"\n            <p>\n              Within the first day of its launch, over 4,000 unique users engaged with Diia.AI, sending over 20,000 messages. Nearly a quarter of the income certificates delivered that day\u2014a highly requested document\u2014were processed through conversations with the AI assistant. Within two weeks, over 20,000 users had sent 64,000 messages, indicating rapid platform adoption.\n            </p>"}},
{type:"text",content:{header:{headline:"<h2>Creating an \u201cairlock\u201d: government-grade data security with Vertex AI</h2>"},body:'\n            <p>\n              Given the agent would be handling Personally Identifiable Information (PII), security and privacy was top priority. Hosting the model on Google\u2019s <a href="https://cloud.google.com/products/agent-builder?hl=en">Vertex AI</a> platform delivered the necessary government-grade security. \u201cWe absolutely could not use any service that would train its models on our users\' queries,\u201d said Ovcharenko, adding, \u201cThe assurance that our data would not be used for training was something that other solutions could not offer with the same level of confidence.\u201d</p><p>The team needed to create an \u201cairlock\u201d between the user\u2019s data and the AI model so the model could work without ever processing raw PII. To handle questions involving PII, they created a unique backend architecture on <a href="https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/">FastAPI</a> and Python, using <a href="https://www.langchain.com/langgraph">LangGraph</a> for orchestration.\n            </p>'}},
{type:"video",content:{video:{sources:[{url:"https://www.gstatic.com/aistudio/case_studies/diia/diiaai_graph.mp4",type:"video/mp4"}],legend:"The diagram shows how PII stays private in an \u201cairlock\u201d system. Once a user initiates a request, it is processed via an Model Context Protocol (MCP), which retrieves data from the state registries. A proprietary PIIManager then acts as an output adapter on top of MCP, ensuring that all responses remain anonymized. Gemini 2.0 Flash then receives this anonymized data and generates a natural response. This response is sent back to the backend, where it is \u201crehydrated\u201d with the original PII before being delivered to the user."}}},
{type:"text",content:{body:"\n            <p>\n              Ovcharenko noted that Gemini helped deliver a service that was previously \u201cimpossible to automate\u201d. Response times come in under the Ministry\u2019s strict sub-2-second Time to First Token (TTFT) target to ensure Diia.AI feels naturally responsive and conversational. The process capitalized on the Gemini model\u2019s speed and excellent Ukrainian understanding to create a highly secure experience without ever coming into contact with raw PII.\n            </p>"}},
{type:"text",content:{header:{headline:"<h2>Broadening features beyond chat</h2>"},body:"\n            <p>\n              The team plans to further refine Diia.AI and integrate it into Diia\u2019s mobile app to further broaden its accessibility. They also have plans to expand the amount of services Diia.AI can offer and introduce new features built with Gemini beyond the chat agent. \u201cThis is just the beginning,\u201d said Dmytro. \u201cWe're not just building an app; we\u2019re building the future of public service.\u201d\n            </p>"}},
{type:"related_cases",content:{mf:["raindrop","instalily","passionfroot"]}}]},{title:"Assort Health",Ue:"Learn how AI agents automate a wide range of patient interactions, leading to lower wait times and increased appointment bookings.",slug:"assorthealth",zf:"https://aistudio.google.com/prompts/new_chat?model=gemini-flash-latest",thumbnail:{url:"https://www.gstatic.com/aistudio/case_studies/assort/Assort_thumbnail.jpg",alt:"Assort Health showcase preview"},se:["Gemini 2.5 Flash"],modules:[{type:"hero",
content:{date:"Dec 30, 2025",headline:"Assort Health improves healthcare access by automating millions of patient calls with Gemini 2.5 Flash",Zq:"Assort Health's AI agents use Gemini 2.5 Flash to handle a wide range of patient interactions, leading to lower wait times and increased appointment bookings.",De:[{name:"Jon Wang",role:"Founder and Co-CEO, Assort Health"},{name:"Jeffery Liu",role:"Founder and Co-CEO, Assort Health"},{name:"Sean Muirhead",role:"Agent Engineering Lead, Assort Health"},{name:"Vishal Dharmadhikari",
role:"Product Solutions Engineer"}],thumbnail:{src:"https://www.gstatic.com/aistudio/case_studies/Assort_Health_hero.jpg",type:"image",alt:"Assort Health showcase hero"}}},{type:"stats",content:{stats:[{value:"5%",description:"Increase in total number of appointments booked"},{value:"89%",description:"Reduction in patient wait times"},{value:"50M+",description:"Interactions averaging a 4.3 / 5 CSAT score"}]}},{type:"cta",content:{link:"https://aistudio.google.com/prompts/new_chat?model=gemini-flash-latest"}},
{type:"text",content:{body:"\n            <p>\n              Imagine having 24/7 access to your healthcare provider. Assort Health is doing just that by revolutionizing patient access and operational efficiency in healthcare with its specialty-trained agentic AI contact center that handles a range of patient interactions.\n            </p>"}},{type:"video",content:{video:{sources:[{url:"https://www.gstatic.com/aistudio/case_studies/assort/assorthealth_diagram.mp4",type:"video/mp4"}],legend:"Simplified visualization for illustrative purposes."}}},
{type:"text",content:{body:"\n            <p>\n              Historically, automating healthcare workflows has been one of the industry\u2019s toughest challenges, especially for specialty-specific tasks that require a deep understanding of the domain. Assort Health has cracked the code on that complexity, leveraging data across thousands of providers and 55 million interactions.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              Agentic state machines work together to navigate complex appointment logic, payer information, and other requirements unique to each specialty. This efficiency has led to a 5% increase in the number of appointments booked while decreasing operational costs by 48% for customers.\n            </p>"}},
{type:"text",content:{header:{headline:"<h2>Implementing Gemini 2.5 Flash for speed and context</h2>"},body:"\n            <p>\n              Assort Health\u2019s platform goes far beyond appointment scheduling to handle the complexities of healthcare:\n            </p>\n              <ul>\n                <li><b>Insurance capture:</b> Accurately recording and verifying insurance information</li>\n                <li><b>Refill requests:</b> Processing medication refill requests efficiently</li>\n                <li><b>Care gap closures:</b> Running proactive campaigns to mitigate surges in demand for care like flu season, closing care gaps and improving population health</li>\n              </ul>\n            <p>\n              The system must accurately account for patient appointment history, chief complaints, insurance details, and medical specialty-specific rules.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              Gemini 2.5 Flash enables Assort Health to manage these complex, latency-sensitive workflows. AI agents can handle a high volume of interactions while maintaining the necessary speed and contextual understanding to ensure a seamless experience. The results are significant: 89% shorter wait times, 81% lower call abandonment rate, and a customer satisfaction (CSAT) score of 4.3/5 from over 50 million patient-agent interactions.\n            </p>"}},
{type:"text",content:{header:{headline:"<h2>Scaling healthcare accessibility</h2>"},body:'\n            <p>\n              Assort Health demonstrates how AI agents can help scale patient access in healthcare. The platform is projected to handle over 100 million interactions by the end of the year and will continue development of specialty-specific AI agents to expand inbound and outbound communications.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              To start building applications with Gemini models, explore our <a href="https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs">API documentation</a>.\n            </p>'}},
{type:"related_cases",content:{mf:["raindrop","passionfroot","calcam"]}}]},{title:"CompScience",Ue:"CompScience analyzes thousands of hours of video footage to improve industrial worksite safety",slug:"compscience",zf:"https://aistudio.google.com/prompts/new_chat?model=gemini-flash-latest",aha:"https://aistudio.google.com/prompts/new_chat?model=gemini-pro-latest",thumbnail:{url:"https://www.gstatic.com/aistudio/case_studies/compScience/CompScience_thumbnail.jpg",alt:"CompScience showcase preview"},
se:["Gemini 2.5 Pro","Gemini 2.5 Flash"],modules:[{type:"hero",content:{date:"Jan 7, 2025",headline:"CompScience improves industrial worksite safety with on-demand image and video analysis",Zq:"CompScience uses Gemini 2.5 Pro and 2.5 Flash to analyze worksite footage and mitigate realtime hazards. Through their Safe Work Plan, Safety Pulse, and Safety Search products, they scale expert knowledge to help workers stay safe on the job.",De:[{name:"Dan Walton",role:"Principal Engineer, CompScience"},
{name:"Vishal Dharmadhikari",role:"Product Solutions Engineer"}],thumbnail:{src:"https://www.gstatic.com/aistudio/case_studies/compScience/CompScience_hero.jpg",type:"image",alt:"CompScience showcase hero"}}},{type:"stats",content:{stats:[{value:"400%",description:"Adoption of Safe Work Plan vs. standard techniques"},{value:"15K+",description:"Hours of video footage processed"},{value:"60",description:"Detailed risk reports deployed to industry"}]}},{type:"cta",content:{link:"https://aistudio.google.com/prompts/new_chat?model=gemini-flash-latest"}},
{type:"text",content:{body:"\n            <p>\n              CompScience is on a mission to eliminate workplace accidents by using AI to provide Safe Work Plans, real-time alerts, and comprehensive safety reports derived from worksite video footage. Partnering with professional risk experts like the National Safety Council, CompScience serves over 100 industrial customers across a variety of sectors, helping them identify risks before they become injuries.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              The core challenge for CompScience is the sheer volume of data. Industrial worksites generate hundreds of hours of video every day. Manually reviewing this footage for potential hazards is impossible at scale. To turn this massive unstructured dataset into concise, actionable safety information, CompScience turned to the Gemini API.\n            </p>"}},
{type:"text",content:{header:{headline:"<h2>Scaling expert safety knowledge with Gemini 2.5 Pro</h2>"},body:"\n            <p>\n              CompScience utilizes Gemini 2.5 Pro to build their Safe Work Plan application. When maintenance workers encounter unplanned work in a factory, they can use their cellphones to take photos of the situation.\n            </p>"}},{type:"images",content:{items:[{image:{src:"https://www.gstatic.com/aistudio/case_studies/compScience/CompScience_inline_01.jpg",alt:"Phone screen allowing users to input job details to conduct a quick Risk Prediction."},
legend:"Workers can submit photos from job sites to generate a Safe Work Plan detailing hazards and proposed safeguards."}]}},{type:"text",content:{body:"\n            <p>\n              2.5 Pro processes these images, reasons through complex safety assessment rubrics, and provides expert-informed advice and guidance. These recommendations can then be saved as standard safe company procedures, effectively digitizing and scaling expert safety knowledge.\n            </p>"}},{type:"text",content:{header:{headline:"<h2>Processing over 15 thousand hours of video with Gemini 2.5 Flash</h2>"},
body:"\n            <p>\n              Beyond static images, CompScience needs to process continuous video streams for their Safety Pulse and Safety Search products. They utilize Gemini 2.5 Flash to periodically assess worksite cameras for immediate issues and to rapidly search through hundreds of hours of archived video in minutes to generate impact reports.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              According to Daniel Walton, Principal Engineer at CompScience, 2.5 Flash\u2019s native video processing capabilities are a key differentiator, noting that \u201cvideo processing just isn\u2019t available\u201d at the same level with other AI providers they tested. To manage the high throughput of video data, CompScience leverages the Files API, using multiple threads to upload video and generate insights efficiently.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              A recent development for CompScience is utilizing Gemini 2.5 Flash\u2019s ability to generate bounding boxes around identified hazards within continuous video or images. This visual grounding allows them to help identify unsafe behaviors or conditions in their reports, a feature Walton notes is \u201conly possible with Gemini 2.5 Flash\u201d for their specific use case.\n            </p>"}},
{type:"images",content:{items:[{image:{src:"https://www.gstatic.com/aistudio/case_studies/compScience/CompScience_inline_02.jpg",alt:'Two screenshots of the CompScience SafetyPulse interface. The left screen shows a video feed from a construction site with a green bounding box around a crane, alongside an "Alert" log identifying a suspended load hazard. A "Take Action" pop-up menu allows users to select corrective measures. The right screen displays a "Safety Overview" dashboard with camera activity thumbnails, alert summaries, and a generated report listing potential safety hazards and recommendations for improvement.'},
legend:"Gemini 2.5 Flash processes job site security photos for safety managers to review, then generates actionable daily reports."}]}},{type:"text",content:{header:{headline:"<h2>Proactively improving safety and mitigating hazards</h2>"},body:"\n            <p>\n              By integrating Gemini models, CompScience currently delivers video-driven safety reports to hundreds of customers. The effectiveness of their AI-driven approach has led the National Safety Council to include the CompScience Safe Work Plan system for their own members, scaling these safety benefits to a broader industrial audience.\n            </p>"}},
